nd the identity labels (detector proposals are not used for ReID training).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Query path:&lt;/b&gt; query crop (256×128) → the same DINOv3 encoder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Legend:&lt;/b&gt; blue = detector, green = ReID, orange = outputs; dashed border = frozen during ReID training. The query is always a GT crop and follows the &lt;i&gt;query path&lt;/i&gt;; the ranking is cosine similarity between L2-normalised 256-d embeddings." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="395" width="1320" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>